# ================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages — routing
# ================================================================
# Intentionally (nearly) empty of rules.
#
# How routing works for this project (Cloudflare Pages, Git integration):
#
#   • A URL that matches a file in dist/ is served as-is, including every
#     prerendered /<route>/index.html (built by vite.config.ts).
#   • A URL that matches nothing falls back to the SPA shell (index.html,
#     200) — this is Pages' automatic SPA behavior and is what makes deep
#     links / client-side routes work.
#   • The one thing the fallback gets wrong — answering a MISSING image or
#     asset (e.g. /img/projects/typo.webp) with the HTML shell instead of a
#     404 — is corrected in `functions/_middleware.js`.
#
# ⚠️ Do NOT add a `/* /index.html 200` rule here. Cloudflare follows
# `_redirects` rules even when a static file exists for the path, so a
# catch-all would clobber the per-route prerendered HTML.
#
# Add only real, permanent redirects below, e.g.:
#   /old-path /new-path 301
# ================================================================
